The Bastion is the neutral elite of the Warden of the Wall (Arbalist route;
no alignment asked). A foe that attacks an ally in its column is answered
with the bolt the Bastion was holding, which unloads the crossbow: the next
turn is a winding.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Covering shot      a loaded crossbow answers a foe that attacks an ally
                        in its column with a bolt at 80% of a blow's damage,
                        twice a battle; the answer unloads it
  35 Keeper's vigor     +14% maximum health in all
  40 Heavy pavise       the row's damage cut is 20%
  45 Third shot         Covering shot works three times a battle
  50 Bastion plate      +8 armor in all
  55 Heavy answer       Covering shot deals a full blow's damage
  60 Unbroken wall      the row's damage cut is 25%

It needs the Warden of the Wall first (<ansi fg="command">help arbalist-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] bastion confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Arbalist talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Long Draw (+10% damage with a
shooting weapon), Eagle Eye (+5 Attack with a shooting weapon), Quick Nock
(starts a battle with 15 points on its action meter). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help arbalist-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help arbalist</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
